  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting Eastern Libya Recovery Through Socio-Economic and Psychosocial Support and Disaster Preparedness in the Aftermath of Storm Daniel</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">On 10 September 2023, Storm Daniel made landfall in Libya causing severe weather conditions, including strong winds and sudden heavy rainfall affecting the northeastern areas of Libya. The storm led to significant infrastructure damage, including road network, disrupted the telecommunications network, and caused large scale displacement. 
 
Through this project, IOM aims to respond to the immediate recovery and reconstruction needs while placing preparedness and prevention at the core of its intervention and to pre-emptively address future hazards through, inter-alia capacity building, stakeholder engagement, and advocacy work. IOM is strengthening the ability of responders and humanitarian actors to respond to and manage disasters, as well as enhance preparedness and coordination capacities. Additionally, IOM is promoting the resilience of flood-affected communities by supporting the health facilities to provide essential healthcare services, and by supporting socio-economic recovery through implementation of Community Improvement Projects (CIPs) and community resilience activities through community resilience activities and improving access to psychosocial support.</narrative>
  </description>
